# Settler Repository Hygiene Rules

## Documentation Standards

- **No markdown files outside `/docs/`** - All documentation must be in the docs folder
- **No markdown files in `/src/`** - Code documentation should use JSDoc comments
- **No scratchpad files** - Temporary notes, ideas, or drafts should not be committed
- **Archive deprecated content** - Move old docs to `/archive/old_docs/`

## File Naming Conventions

- **kebab-case** for files (e.g., `api-quick-start.md`, `user-service.ts`)
- **PascalCase** for components (e.g., `UserProfile.tsx`, `PaymentForm.tsx`)
- **Numbered prefixes** for sequential docs (e.g., `00-intro.md`, `01-architecture.md`)
- **Meaningful names** - Avoid cryptic or abbreviated filenames

## Code Organization

- **No dead code** - Remove unused components, functions, and imports
- **No commented-out code** - Remove unless explicitly marked "preserve"
- **Consistent formatting** - Use Prettier and ESLint
- **Clear comments** - Comments should explain "why", not "what"

## Business Documents

- **Internal docs** - `/docs/internal/business-strategy.md` (single canonical file)
- **External docs** - `/docs/external/product-overview.md` (single canonical file)
- **No duplicates** - Archive or merge duplicate business documents

## Archive Structure

- `/archive/deprecated_code/` - Unused code modules
- `/archive/old_docs/` - Deprecated documentation
- `/archive/legacy_designs/` - Old design files
- `/archive/experiments/` - Experimental code
- `/archive/unused_assets/` - Unused assets

## Branch Management

- **Delete merged branches** - Clean up merged feature branches
- **Delete abandoned branches** - Remove WIP branches older than 90 days
- **Keep active branches** - Only preserve branches with real work-in-progress

## Security

- **No secrets in code** - Use environment variables
- **No API keys** - Store in `.env` files (gitignored)
- **Encrypt sensitive docs** - Use git-crypt for internal business documents

## Build & Quality

- **All builds must pass** - Type checks, linting, tests
- **No broken imports** - Ensure all imports resolve after restructuring
- **Documentation links** - All links in docs must work

## Enforcement

- **Pre-commit hooks** - Run linting and formatting
- **CI/CD checks** - Enforce standards in GitHub Actions
- **Regular audits** - Monthly cleanup of deprecated content

## AI & Architectural Tone

- **No AI slop** - Use professional, concise language. No chatty filler ("Certainly!", "As an AI"), no over-commenting basic syntax, no generic placeholders.
- **Enterprise-Grade** - Produce high-quality, robust, and maintainable code following strict SOLID and deterministic principles.
- **Seed-Ready & Cost-Effective** - Favor highly pragmatic, scalable-to-zero infrastructure. Avoid over-engineered abstractions.
- **Professional Messaging** - All copy, docs, and repo content must be crisp, confident, and professional.
